  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Govt to assess pros and cons of airport operators holding airline stakes",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/industry/aviation/govt-to-assess-pros-and-cons-of-airport-operators-holding-airline-stakes-126092200940_1.html",
      "description": "The government will assess the \"pros and cons\" of the proposal for airport operators owning stakes in airlines and decide on a balanced approach, Civil Aviation Minister K Rammohan Naidu said on Tuesday.\nTalking to reporters on the sidelines of signing pacts for the next phase of Udaan, the minister said that to make full use of today's strong travel demand, India's aviation sector needs at least five airlines operating with 100 aircraft each.\nHe said the ministry is actively supporting the ambition given the country's size and growing airport network.\nNaidu further said people, even in small towns, want airports in their vicinity.\n\"So, it is important for us to plan not only for the aspirations today, but for Viksit Bharat 2047 also,\" he said, adding that India should ideally have more than 350 airports.\nTo a query on the Adani Group seeking to own a stake in an airline, the minister said one thing from the government is clear: the country needs more airlines to come into the ...",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-22T14:17:38"
    },
    {
      "title": "No decision yet on operators of airports owning airlines, says Naidu",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/industry/aviation/no-decision-yet-on-airport-operators-owning-airlines-aviation-minister-126092201196_1.html",
      "description": "Aviation Minister Rammohan Naidu says the government is weighing the pros and cons of relaxing cross-ownership restrictions as it seeks to increase airline choices",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-22T13:58:08"
    }
  ]
